§ `ss 6 item 1, 29, 32`

#ASSERT `contravenes s 29` `k063: the unlicensed lender to Jake's friend`
#ASSERT `contravenes s 29` `k063: the man who glued the lock, collecting for that lender`
#ASSERT NOT `contravenes s 29` `an employee of a licensed lender collecting within authority`
#ASSERT NOT `contravenes s 29` `a friend who lends without charge and not in business`

#ASSERT `s 32 forbids it to take any fee from the consumer` `k063: the unlicensed lender to Jake's friend`

§ `s 180`

#ASSERT `the court may make an order under s 180, including refusing to enforce the contract` `k063: the friend applies on 1 March 2037`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make an order under s 180, including refusing to enforce the contract` `k063: Jake's household applies, not being the borrower`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make an order under s 180, including refusing to enforce the contract` `k063: the friend applies on the sixth anniversary`

§ `Code s 5`

#ASSERT `the National Credit Code applies` `c052: Chloe and Liam's home loan, 500000 to buy the home they will live in`
#ASSERT NOT `the National Credit Code applies` `a loan to Jake's delivery business, half of it for personal use`
#ASSERT `the National Credit Code applies` `k063: the friend's 5000 loan from a lender in business`

§ `Code ss 7, 42, 43`

#ASSERT NOT `the Code makes the mortgage unenforceable` `c052: the mortgage of the Byford house, a separate signed document`
#ASSERT `the Code makes the mortgage unenforceable` `a mortgage the mortgagors never signed`

#ASSERT `days the credit provider has to give the mortgagor a copy` `c052: the mortgage of the Byford house, a separate signed document` EQUALS 14

§ `ss 128-130`

#ASSERT `s 128 is satisfied` `c043: the card issuer's assessment of Chloe 10 days before`
#ASSERT `s 128 is satisfied` `an assessment exactly 90 days old`
#ASSERT NOT `s 128 is satisfied` `an assessment 91 days old`
#ASSERT NOT `s 128 is satisfied` `an assessment without verifying the financial situation`
#ASSERT `s 128 is satisfied` `k049: the payday lender's assessment of Jake with 90 days of statements`
#ASSERT NOT `s 128 is satisfied` `k049 variant: only 30 days of statements`

§ `ss 131, 133`

#ASSERT NOT `the contract is unsuitable under s 131(2) and s 133(2)` `c043: Chloe on 70000, a 6000 card limit she could repay 9000 of in the ASIC period`
#ASSERT `the contract is unsuitable under s 131(2) and s 133(2)` `k048: Jake's second card, a 10000 limit he could repay only 7000 of in the ASIC period`
#ASSERT `the contract is unsuitable under s 131(2) and s 133(2)` `a loan payable only by selling the home`
#ASSERT NOT `the contract is unsuitable under s 131(2) and s 133(2)` `a loan payable only by selling the home, the contrary of hardship proved`
#ASSERT `the contract is unsuitable under s 131(2) and s 133(2)` `a loan that does not meet the consumer's objectives`

#ASSERT `s 133 forbids entering the contract or increasing the limit` `k048: Jake's second card, a 10000 limit he could repay only 7000 of in the ASIC period`
#ASSERT NOT `s 133 forbids entering the contract or increasing the limit` `an unsuitable loan that a regulation takes not to be unsuitable`

#ASSERT `the licensee may enter the contract` `c043: the card issuer's assessment of Chloe 10 days before` `c043: Chloe on 70000, a 6000 card limit she could repay 9000 of in the ASIC period`
#ASSERT NOT `the licensee may enter the contract` `c043: the card issuer's assessment of Chloe 10 days before` `k048: Jake's second card, a 10000 limit he could repay only 7000 of in the ASIC period`

§ `s 132`

#ASSERT `business days to give a copy of the assessment` 20240610 20250610 EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `business days to give a copy of the assessment` 20240610 20260610 EQUALS 21
#ASSERT `business days to give a copy of the assessment` 20240610 20310611 EQUALS 0

§ `s 133BE`

#ASSERT `s 133BE forbids the communication` `k048: a letter to Jake offering a higher limit on his card`
#ASSERT `s 133BE forbids the communication` `an email to Jake meant to get him to ask for more`

§ `s 5 definitions, s 133CA`

#ASSERT `is a small amount credit contract` `k049: Jake's 2000 loan for 12 months at the caps`
#ASSERT `is a small amount credit contract` `k049 as the scenario's list has it: 400 a month on 2000`
#ASSERT `is a small amount credit contract` `a 2000 loan refinancing another small amount loan`
#ASSERT NOT `is a small amount credit contract` `a 2001 loan`
#ASSERT NOT `is a small amount credit contract` `a 2000 loan for 15 days`
#ASSERT NOT `is a small amount credit contract` `a 2000 loan secured on Jake's car`
#ASSERT NOT `is a small amount credit contract` `a bank's 2000 personal loan`

#ASSERT `is a short-term credit contract` `a 2000 loan for 15 days`

§ `Code ss 23A, 31A, 31B, 39B`

#ASSERT `the largest permitted establishment fee` `k049: Jake's 2000 loan for 12 months at the caps` EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `the largest permitted establishment fee` `a 2000 loan refinancing another small amount loan` EQUALS 0

#ASSERT `the largest permitted monthly fee` `k049: Jake's 2000 loan for 12 months at the caps` EQUALS 80

#ASSERT `the most the permitted establishment and monthly fees can come to` `k049: Jake's 2000 loan for 12 months at the caps` 12 EQUALS 1360

#ASSERT `the charges comply with ss 23A and 31A` `k049: Jake's 2000 loan for 12 months at the caps`
#ASSERT NOT `the charges comply with ss 23A and 31A` `k049 as the scenario's list has it: 400 a month on 2000`
#ASSERT NOT `the charges comply with ss 23A and 31A` `a 2000 loan charging 40 of interest`

#ASSERT `the amount the debtor is not liable to pay` `k049: Jake's 2000 loan for 12 months at the caps` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the amount the debtor is not liable to pay` `k049 as the scenario's list has it: 400 a month on 2000` EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `the amount the debtor is not liable to pay` `a 2000 loan with an establishment fee of 500` EQUALS 500

#ASSERT `the most recoverable after a default, before enforcement expenses` `k049: Jake's 2000 loan for 12 months at the caps` EQUALS 4000

